Whenever I hear anb anti-WoW post, it always reminds me of my first few games
of nethack... I was "lucky" enough to find a wow. So, what did I wish for? 
+3 GoP, RoR, and a SoG. At the time, I had no knowledge of things like bPYEC,
GDSM, or any of that stuff... Heck, I didn't even know about blessed/rustproof!
Only through many games did I eventually figure out the things to wish for. 
I don't consider this bad.

Unfortunately, you have the case where people know everything before even
playing the game. oh, well. Not much you can do about it.

The upshot is, wishes are only as effective as your knowledge. And without
spoilers, etc, it takes quite a while to get that knowledge. I personally
still haven't won the damn game yet, and I'm pretty sure I have a good 
knowledge of things I can do. Oh, well. I'll keephacking. I wonder what
would happen if monsters could use WoW? I think It'd be pretty neat :)

